>> title: Lazy Apple Pie Pull-Apart Bread
>> servings: 8

== Filling ==

In a #medium sauce pan{}, cook @apples{3}(peeled and diced) with @butter{2%tbsp}, @brown sugar{0.33%cup}, @cinnamon{1%tsp}, @nutmeg{.25%tsp}, @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, and @salt{pinch} for ~{6-8%minutes}. Mix @cornstarch{1%tbsp} with @water{2%tbsp} and stir in, then cook for ~{1-2%minutes} more until think. Stir in @vanilla{1%tsp} and let cool.

== Cinnamon Sugar ==

In a #small bowl{}, mix together @white sugar{1%cup} and @cinnamon{1%tbsp}. Set aside.

== Making the Bread ==

Preheat an oven to 350F.

In a #small bowl{}, melt @butter{1.5%stick}. Set aside.

Split each @biscuit{1%can, refrigerated} in half, to create two thinner pieces. 

Dip each biscuit half in melted butter then sprinkle cinnamon sugar over each side to coat.

> If there is a little extra apple filling, you can spoon it over the top. 

Assemble biscuits into a stack of 4 or 5, with a spoonful of apple filling between each biscuit. Layer each stack in a #loaf pan{}, lined with parchment paper, with apple filling between each stack in the loaf pan.

> I recommend putting a sheet pan on the level below the loaf pan while baking to catch anything that drips.

Bake at 350F for ~{1%hour}. 